
Dash board creation answer-
“Yes, I have created Grafana dashboards by configuring Prometheus as a data source and writing PromQL queries,or by importing existing dashboards 
using Grafana dashboard IDs.

Prometheus scrapes metrics from exporters such as node-exporter, kube-state-metrics, and blackbox exporter.

We define Prometheus rules in separate YAML files—both recording rules to pre-compute frequently used metrics for performance and 
alerting rules to continuously evaluate conditions like sustained CPU or memory pressure. These rule files are referenced from prometheus.yml.

When an alerting rule fires, Prometheus sends the alert to Alertmanager along with labels such as pod, namespace, and severity.
Alertmanager then handles grouping, deduplication, and routing of notifications to channels like Slack, PagerDuty, or email
so the on-call engineer can take action.”
