tell about your self:day to day tasks of SRE
____________________
In production, we perform regular health checks using monitoring tools llike prometheus & Grafana
Daily, I monitor Grafana dashboards to verify:

Node health
Pod status
CPU, memory, and disk utilization
Service availability
Storage performance

I receive alerts from PagerDuty and Slack and prioritize incidents based on severity and business impact.

When an incident occurs,alerts typically include details such as pod name, namespace, severity level, and error information.
I securely access the Kubernetes cluster through a bastion host and troubleshoot issues using commands
like kubectl describe and kubectl logs, and then take appropriate corrective actions.” 
for example:
if a pod is in a CrashLoopBackOff or OOMKilled state, I analyze the pod events and logs to identify the root cause.
Based on the findings,

I update resource requests and limits,to allocate sufficient memory and prevent future crashes.
Optimize HPA thresholds  based on CPU/memory utilization patterns. or 
Scale pods horizontally or nodes vertically based on workload demand

During deployments, I closely monitor canary releases. If I notice 5xx errors or latency spikes, I immediately rollback and collaborate 
with developers to fix the issue.



Weekly and monthly, I review memory utilization, backup status,security patch compliance,and perform DR drills to 
ensure high availability and business continuity.


After every incident, I perform Root Cause Analysis (RCA) by documenting incident summary, root cause, 
impact analysis, corrective actions, and preventive measures.
 I continuously update runbooks with troubleshooting steps, alert handling procedures, rollback processes, and 
lessons learned from incidents.

 As an SRE we focus on  minimizing MTTR(mean time toi recovery), preventing recurring incidents, 
and improving system reliability through proactive monitoring and automation.”









